  "summary": "I worked through all 13 results inbox items: the 8 that were there when I started and 5 that arrived while I was working. Twelve are closed. One stays open on purpose. There are two loose ends I couldn't close myself (see the end).\n\n**Original 8 items**\n- **Raj Patel (pt-0006), CT urogram 10/19:** no kidney or bladder cause for the hematuria. The 4 mm left lower lobe nodule is the one already followed in lung screening. I first ordered his annual low-dose CT for Mar–May 2027, with a tracking task, a patient message and a note. This was later changed (see below).\n- **pt-0016, TSH:** normal; closed.\n- **pt-0016, potassium:** the lab corrected 6.3 to 4.4 (analyzer fault); closed with no action.\n- **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), preliminary CTA chest:** the final report says no clot in the lungs, and the \"nodule\" is a blood vessel. It says no follow-up imaging is needed, so I closed it.\n- **pt-0064, St. Brigid creatinine 1.36 (9/26):** no comparison value in the prior 48 h or 7 days, so it doesn't count as acute kidney injury; closed.\n- **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), BMP 10/22:** acute kidney injury (creatinine 0.98 to 1.64 in 35 h, after IV contrast and NSAIDs). I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by 10/26, put his naproxen on hold, messaged him today (stop ibuprofen and naproxen) and wrote a note.\n- **Carol Whitfield (pt-0033), creatinine 1.31:** the 10/21 value was entered in error and was excluded. Compared with 1.27 on 10/17 it doesn't count as kidney injury; closed.\n- **Walter Brennan (pt-0008), potassium 6.4 flagged hemolyzed:** I ordered an urgent repeat BMP and messaged him to come in. This was escalated later (see below).\n\n**5 items that arrived while I worked**\n- **Walter Brennan:** the lab corrected the result. The hemolysis comment belonged to another patient's sample, so the 6.4 is real. I sent a stat message to the on-call pool, ordered a stat BMP for today and sent him a corrected message to come in today. None of his medicines raise potassium. Note written.\n- **Carol Whitfield, urgent care creatinine 1.78 (10/22 evening):** up 0.47 from 1.31 nine hours earlier, so this is acute kidney injury. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by 10/26, messaged her today and wrote a note. Her hydrochlorothiazide and insulin are flagged in the note for you to review.\n- **pt-0064, creatinine 1.48:** no comparison value in the window, so it doesn't count as kidney injury and needs no action under the policy; closed. It is above her 0.9 baseline, so it's worth rechecking at her next visit.\n- **Raj Patel, outside addendum to his 4/14 screening CT:** a new 5 mm right upper lobe nodule, rated probably benign, with a repeat scan advised at 6 months. I ordered the low-dose CT for now through 11/14 with a tracking task, sent him a corrected message and wrote a note explaining the change.\n- **Leslie Parisian, preliminary chest X-ray 10/22 (possible 7 mm nodule):** no final report yet, so per policy this item stays open.\n\n**What still needs you**\n- **Cancel the 2027 lung CT order for Raj Patel (sr-t0001) and its tracking task (task-t0002).** My tools can't cancel orders or tasks. I left a task for you (task-t0032), due 10/26.\n- **Ignore Walter Brennan's urgent BMP order (sr-t0016).** The stat BMP replaces it, and I couldn't cancel it either.\n- **Raj Patel has an open hemolyzed potassium of 6.3 from 10/21** in Dr. Reyes's inbox, not yours. The answering service couldn't reach the covering clinician. I messaged Dr. Reyes about it.\n- **Smoking history doesn't match across records** for Raj Patel and Leslie Parisian; neither plan changes because of it.\n- **Your messages inbox has 6 refill requests** I didn't touch, since you asked about results.",
